# Source: Wikipedia summary
# Topic: Databases
T:Databases
T:Reference
T:Category
T:Computers
T:------------
T:What it is
T:In
T:computing, a
T:database is
T:an organized
T:collection
T:of data or a
T:type of data
T:store based
T:on the use
T:of a
T:database
T:management
T:system
T:(DBMS), the
T:software
T:that
T:interacts
T:with end
T:users,
T:application,
T:and the
T:database
T:itself to
T:capture and
T:analyze the
T:data. The
T:DBMS
T:additionally
T:encompasses
T:the core
T:facilities
T:provided to
T:administer
T:the
T:database.
T:The sum
T:total of the
T:database,
T:the DBMS and
T:the
T:associated
T:applications
T:can be
T:referred to
T:as a
T:database
T:system.
T:Often the
T:term
T:"database"
T:is also used
T:loosely to
T:refer to any
T:of the DBMS,
T:the database
T:system or an
T:application
T:associated
T:with the
T:database.
